## 8. Testing & measurement

1. **Chrome DevTools** — mobile trace: identify LCP element, load delay vs duration
2. **Network** — Slow 4G; confirm preloads fire before LCP image; woff2 not woff
3. **Console** — no 404 on `assets/*.js` referenced from Liquid
4. **Block test** — block `googletagmanager.com`; if TBT unchanged, theme work is sufficient; if TBT drops, marketing stack is next bottleneck
5. **Build** — `climaybe build` before ship

### Template LCP candidates (verify per store)

| Template | Typical LCP element |
|----------|---------------------|
| Index | Hero background (`m--hero-wrapper` / `a--image-responsive`) |
| Collection | First grid product card OR `collection.image` on model template |
| Product | First gallery slider image |

---

## 9. Known pitfalls (from production)

1. **Standalone script tags for bundled modules** — 404 + MIME type errors (`sticky-atc.js`, etc.)
2. **Global helpers across bundles** — `fetchConfig` pattern failed after JS split; use inline fetch or explicit imports within the same entry
3. **Lazysizes leftovers** — `data-srcset` + 20px `src` causes pixelated LCP
4. **Oversized mobile srcset** — 3x retina on heroes; use `three_x_retina_mobile: false`
5. **Preload mismatch** — preload 420w but img requests 1260w → load delay unchanged
6. **GTM double-load** — theme + Customer Events same container ID
7. **`{% for %}` split across liquid tags** — Liquid syntax errors; keep loops in one block
8. **Font repo drift** — all woff2 files must exist in `assets/` for CI/deploy parity

